WEBVTT

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:06.860
The session is over. Now the real work begins.

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:11.320
Here’s how to make sure what you agreed actually changes how you work.

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:13.940
First, write it up within a day.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:19.220
Not a long report: just the canvas, and a short list of agreements and next steps.

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:22.760
Share it with everyone, and put it somewhere people will see it.

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:25.940
A printed canvas on the wall works surprisingly well.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.420
Online, pin it in your team channel.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:32.740
Second, use it. Refer to the canvas in normal work.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:35.680
When a decision comes up, check the decision rules.

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:39.700
When someone new joins, walk them through the canvas in their first week.

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.140
When a behaviour from the contract is broken, point to it.

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:46.160
Every time you use it, it becomes more real.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:48.800
Third, follow up on actions.

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:53.180
Put them on your normal task list, not in a separate document nobody opens.

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:58.280
At your next team meeting, spend two minutes on: “How are we doing with what we agreed?”

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:01.000
Fourth, notice what changes.

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:05.680
After a few weeks, ask the team: “What’s different since we had this conversation?”

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:07.480
Celebrate the small things.

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:10.920
It shows people that these conversations are worth their time.

00:01:10.970 --> 00:01:16.920
And remember the thing you wrote down in the very first lesson: what you wanted to be different in three months.

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:18.868
Look at it now and then. Is it changing?

